# SPA fallback for Netlify-class static hosting.
#
# Without this file, the host may fall back to serving dist/index.html for
# every path regardless of whether a matching prerendered file exists (e.g.
# dist/about/index.html, dist/travel-tips/<slug>/index.html) — which is what
# was happening in production: every route showed the homepage's title/
# description/OG tags to crawlers, even though prerender-seo.mjs generates a
# correct file per route at build time.
#
# This rule only catches paths with NO matching static file. Netlify's static
# asset resolution checks for a real file at the exact path first (that's
# default behavior, not something this file controls), so an existing
# dist/about/index.html is still served for /about — this line only supplies
# the fallback for genuinely unknown routes, so React Router can render the
# client-side NotFound page instead of a bare host 404.
#
# Status 404 (not 200): Netlify's _redirects lets a rewrite still serve the
# SPA shell while returning a real HTTP status other than 200 — confirmed via
# curl that every genuinely unknown path was returning 200 OK (a soft-404),
# which search engines can index as if it were real content. Every legitimate
# route already has its own prerendered file matched before this rule is ever
# reached, so there's no route that needs the 200 behavior.
/*   /index.html   404
